  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing support to Vietnam for the implementation of the Paris Agreement.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam is pursuing a dedicated climate policy. The country was one of the first nations to draw up an action plan to implement the Paris Agreement. The project supported the Vietnamese government in creating the framework conditions for the implementation of the Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) and the Paris Agreement. The focus was on advising the Ministry of Environment (MONRE) on the development of the NDCs, the establishment of an institutional framework for the implementation of the Paris Agreement and the development of Nationally Appropriate Mitigation Actions (NAMAs) . The project also developed mitigation measures and carried out adaptation measures in two provinces. These measures were extended to other areas and both contributed to achieving the Vietnamese NDCs. The programme also coordinated the &#x201c;IKI Interface for Vietnam&#x201d;, which, among other tasks, networks the IKI projects in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
